  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The federal market for Electrical Contractors and Other Wiring Installation Contractors (NAICS 238210) shows $501M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date, with 2,139 awards and an average award size of $234K. Obligations are down 36.6% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows FY21 obligations at $792M, FY22 at $853M, FY23 at $945M, FY24 at $824M, FY25 at $791M, and FY26 at $501M. The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $134M in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs with $114M and the Department of State with $87.6M. Top vendors in FY2026 to date include XATOR LLC with $58.9M, SINTELA INC with $36.3M, and WSP USA SOLUTIONS INC with $32.9M. This slice of the market reflects concentrated buying by a handful of agencies and vendors, and a notable year-over-year decline in obligations through the current fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "?Who are the biggest buyers right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the biggest buyer with $134M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $114M, and the Department of State follows with $87.6M. The Department of Transportation and the Department of Homeland Security round out the next largest buyers with $60.7M and $41.7M respectively."
      },
